WEBVTT

02:11.020 --> 02:12.020
Fire Lance!

02:28.530 --> 02:29.420
Sei!

03:28.110 --> 03:31.920
<i>It's been three months since I returned 
to the royal capital from Klausner's Domain.</i>

03:32.550 --> 03:35.020
<i>Summertime is almost upon us.</i>

03:35.610 --> 03:38.380
<i>This will be my second summer in this world.</i>

03:39.770 --> 03:41.240
<i>Following my return,</i>

03:41.240 --> 03:45.660
<i>the royal palace has sent me 
to various areas to dispatch monsters.</i>

03:45.660 --> 03:50.080
<i>At present, we've purified
all known miasma swamps.</i>

03:50.460 --> 03:54.000
<i>And thankfully,
the purified regions have all seen</i>

03:54.000 --> 03:59.360
<i>a significant decrease in monsters.</i>

04:00.340 --> 04:05.400
<i>I've settled into this routine
of investigation and purification.</i>

04:06.300 --> 04:11.930
<i>Although, since the knights take care
of the regions without miasma swamps,</i>

04:11.930 --> 04:14.770
<i>I've actually had a bit of free time lately.</i>

04:15.170 --> 04:16.980
<i>And one day...</i>

04:19.410 --> 04:20.320
We need help!

04:20.320 --> 04:21.190
Yes!

04:25.110 --> 04:28.120
"The Trading Company"

04:29.250 --> 04:31.070
What a haul!

04:34.250 --> 04:37.000
What's all this? There's so much stuff...

04:37.000 --> 04:39.500
Oh, Sei. Good morning.

04:39.500 --> 04:42.050
Good morning. What's going on here?

04:42.050 --> 04:45.400
We received all of this from 
Klausner's Domain early this morning.

04:45.400 --> 04:46.980
From Klausner's Domain?

04:46.980 --> 04:51.630
Indeed. But it's a little too much...

05:01.600 --> 05:02.360
Sei.

05:04.520 --> 05:06.530
Your share is over there.

05:08.380 --> 05:09.490
Yup.

05:18.040 --> 05:20.520
This is all for me?

05:20.520 --> 05:21.800
Apparently so.

05:21.800 --> 05:23.630
What's it doing here?

05:23.630 --> 05:25.050
It had your name on it.

05:25.050 --> 05:27.390
Since we don't know what's inside,

05:27.390 --> 05:31.760
we couldn't just leave it in the storehouse 
where anyone could open it.

05:31.760 --> 05:33.470
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

05:33.940 --> 05:36.240
Here. There's a letter, too.

05:40.150 --> 05:43.320
<i>It's been a long time, Sei. 
I hope you're doing well.</i>

05:43.730 --> 05:45.730
<i>Things are the same as ever here.</i>

05:45.730 --> 05:52.140
<i>Even after your departure, those fools keep 
demanding a stupid number of potions.</i>

05:52.140 --> 05:54.600
<i>I swear, there's no end of trouble.</i>

05:55.580 --> 06:01.540
<i>Nevertheless, I thought it would be 
tough to replant all those herbs</i>

06:01.540 --> 06:05.720
<i>and tend to the forest 
destroyed by slimes, and yet...</i>

06:06.290 --> 06:12.000
<i>I don't know how, but the forest 
has returned to its verdant glory.</i>

06:12.330 --> 06:14.770
<i>In fact, it's recovered even more than that.</i>

06:14.770 --> 06:19.670
<i>I've been able to collect herbs 
that used to be so hard to find!</i>

06:19.670 --> 06:26.790
<i>I just have </i>no idea<i> who might have 
been kind enough to help us out so,</i>

06:26.790 --> 06:28.990
<i>but I'm dearly grateful for it.</i>

06:28.990 --> 06:31.810
<i>Well then, be sure to visit us again.</i>

06:31.810 --> 06:34.390
<i>I'll be waiting. Sincerely, Corinna.</i>

06:35.410 --> 06:36.370
What does it say?

06:36.370 --> 06:39.270
It's a thank-you letter 
for dispatching the monsters.

06:39.270 --> 06:42.000
It seems the herbs are a gift.

06:42.000 --> 06:45.840
I see. You must have gone overboard again.

06:46.240 --> 06:47.710
How rude.

06:47.710 --> 06:49.170
That's not true...

06:49.170 --> 06:51.890
<i>At least, I don't think so.</i>

06:51.890 --> 06:54.350
I'm no less suspicious.

06:56.380 --> 07:00.920
Well, either way, it looks like we'll be able
 to make some real headway in our work.

07:00.920 --> 07:04.990
A lot of research projects have
been on hold due to the herb shortage.

07:04.990 --> 07:09.010
Yes, I'd like some
of this gift to use right away

07:09.010 --> 07:11.780
on the new cosmetics I'm making.

07:14.050 --> 07:16.430
New cosmetics?

07:16.430 --> 07:17.620
Is there a problem?

07:18.110 --> 07:19.330
Er, no.

07:19.330 --> 07:21.750
Do you intend to sell them
through the trading company?

07:22.330 --> 07:25.580
I wasn't really planning 
on selling the products.

07:25.580 --> 07:28.800
I see. Very well, then.

07:30.820 --> 07:32.680
But if you're the one making them,

07:32.680 --> 07:35.470
I'm sure there are people 
who'd love to buy them.

07:39.680 --> 07:41.020
<b>Everyone
would
love
them!</b>

07:41.350 --> 07:41.790
<b>Me too!</b>

07:41.540 --> 07:42.080
<b>Lady Sei!</b>

07:41.730 --> 07:42.290
<b>Me too!</b>

07:41.910 --> 07:42.330
<b>Lady Sei!</b>

07:42.040 --> 07:42.330
<b>Me too!</b>

07:42.980 --> 07:43.900
<b>SIIIIIGH</b>

07:44.270 --> 07:45.400
<b>Eh heh heh heh heh heh heh</b>

07:45.610 --> 07:46.650
<b>SPARKLE
SPARKLE\h\h\h</b>

07:47.400 --> 07:48.230
<b>TA-DA</b>

07:50.260 --> 07:51.820
I suppose.

07:52.610 --> 07:57.690
I should get advice from the trading 
company I worked with last time.

07:57.690 --> 08:01.060
Yes, they'll be the ones
making and selling the products

08:01.060 --> 08:02.520
based on your recipes.

08:03.920 --> 08:07.700
I'll go ahead and contact them for you.

08:07.700 --> 08:09.250
I appreciate it.

08:09.250 --> 08:13.380
In the meantime,
we need to store all this somewhere else.

08:13.380 --> 08:16.300
My apologies for the trouble.

08:16.830 --> 08:18.100
Right back at you.

08:18.100 --> 08:18.940
Huh?

08:18.940 --> 08:21.850
You were suddenly summoned to our world

08:21.850 --> 08:26.560
and you've worked hard for 
our kingdom without complaint.

08:27.290 --> 08:29.660
This is the least I can do.

08:32.610 --> 08:34.600
Thank you for always helping me.

08:50.990 --> 08:55.220
You seem like you've grown
accustomed to dressing.

08:55.220 --> 08:57.520
K-Kind of you to say so...

08:59.300 --> 09:02.960
If I may ask, what are these, Lady Sei?

09:04.270 --> 09:08.230
Oh, those are new cosmetics 
I'm working on right now.

09:09.230 --> 09:12.310
Did you say new cosmetics, my lady?

09:12.310 --> 09:16.200
Yes, I'm researching a cream 
that can beautify your skin.

09:17.410 --> 09:19.660
Beautify your skin?

09:19.660 --> 09:23.140
What a splendid and noble project.

09:23.140 --> 09:24.370
Lady Sei!

09:25.500 --> 09:26.830
Huh... Wh-What?

09:25.500 --> 09:27.440
Please show me, too!

09:27.440 --> 09:28.290
It beautifies skin?!

09:28.290 --> 09:29.750
Please show me!

09:29.750 --> 09:31.210
Me too, Lady Sei!

09:31.210 --> 09:33.420
Pipe down now, girls!

09:36.990 --> 09:39.970
How dare you act so shamelessly
 in front of Lady Sei!

09:41.640 --> 09:43.950
It's still a work in progress,

09:43.950 --> 09:46.650
but I'd like you all to try it out for me
 after I make sure

09:46.650 --> 09:49.190
it's safe to use by testing it on myself.

09:49.190 --> 09:51.900
I'll be counting on you then.

09:53.360 --> 09:54.630
Of course!

09:54.630 --> 09:56.260
Please let us help!

09:56.260 --> 09:57.580
I'd be happy to!

09:57.580 --> 09:59.070
That's our Lady Sei!

10:05.930 --> 10:07.230
May I come in?

10:07.230 --> 10:08.960
Yes, we've been expecting you.

10:21.450 --> 10:23.180
Sorry to call you so early.

10:23.180 --> 10:24.070
It's nothing...

10:24.070 --> 10:26.140
Meet Franz and Oscar.

10:26.140 --> 10:29.230
Nice to meet you. My name is Franz.

10:29.230 --> 10:30.450
And I'm Oscar.

10:30.450 --> 10:31.690
It's nice to meet you.

10:31.980 --> 10:34.720
It's nice to meet you, too. I'm Sei.

10:42.340 --> 10:47.940
I called you here to talk about 
starting your own trading company.

10:47.940 --> 10:49.880
You mean one for myself?

10:49.880 --> 10:51.130
That's right.

10:51.130 --> 10:54.410
Remember the cosmetics you created before?

10:54.410 --> 10:59.260
They're being handled
by the trading company my family runs.

10:59.260 --> 11:03.180
Your products are incredible hits
and have the potential

11:03.180 --> 11:08.790
to garner both unbelievable
popularity and profits.

11:08.790 --> 11:12.020
Since your products are so beloved,

11:12.020 --> 11:15.360
other trading companies
are giving the current operation grief.

11:15.840 --> 11:20.240
I've heard that there are so 
many orders from the nobility

11:20.240 --> 11:24.320
that Count Valdec himself
had to step in to mediate.

11:24.750 --> 11:26.490
I had no idea...

11:26.490 --> 11:29.160
Don't worry about it. It's not your fault.

11:29.570 --> 11:34.190
However, we can't release your new 
product under the circumstances.

11:34.190 --> 11:40.500
You should create your own trading company
to be the sole distributor of your products.

11:41.780 --> 11:48.210
But can this really be solved just by
selling the products under a different name?

11:48.210 --> 11:51.350
Who would dare interfere
with an operation run by the Saint?

11:51.350 --> 11:53.370
<i>Wait, is that the deal?</i>

11:53.370 --> 11:55.340
Indeed, indeed.

11:58.170 --> 12:01.370
But Director, even if the trading 
company is under my name,

12:01.370 --> 12:03.950
all I know how to do is develop new products.

12:03.950 --> 12:07.030
I know. That's why these two are here.

12:07.340 --> 12:12.500
You just need to keep creating
new products as you think of them.

12:12.500 --> 12:19.080
With your permission, we would like
to take care of running your storefronts,

12:19.080 --> 12:23.970
preparing other items,
and managing the inventory.

12:23.970 --> 12:27.090
Goodness, in that case, I really don't mind.

12:27.090 --> 12:29.930
I'd be very grateful for the help...

12:32.340 --> 12:33.600
Then it's decided.

12:34.290 --> 12:36.830
I'll be counting on you from now on.

12:37.830 --> 12:41.680
We're looking forward
to working with you, my lady.

13:11.490 --> 13:13.100
It seems to be a success.

13:13.100 --> 13:17.390
It certainly is. 
Your cosmetics are quite popular, Lady Sei.

13:17.390 --> 13:21.690
I heard that only nobles 
were buying them before.

13:21.690 --> 13:24.060
That's because we couldn't
keep up with demand.

13:24.060 --> 13:28.590
I'm told that's why we marketed
the products exclusively to nobles.

13:28.960 --> 13:32.160
But even so, they're famous
 among merchant families.

13:32.160 --> 13:35.370
<i>Huh, so that's the real story.</i>

13:35.370 --> 13:41.190
So I'm glad we were able to expand 
our demographic with your idea, Lady Sei.

13:41.190 --> 13:43.090
Franz was appreciative as well.

13:43.490 --> 13:48.430
<i>It's really easy to talk to Oscar
because he isn't so stuffy.</i>

13:48.840 --> 13:50.550
I see. That's good to hear.

13:50.550 --> 13:52.020
And what idea was that?

13:52.830 --> 13:55.220
A new way to sell our products.

13:55.620 --> 14:00.690
She suggested offering cosmetics 
with differing levels of efficacy.

14:03.450 --> 14:05.540
Is everything going well at the store?

14:05.540 --> 14:08.890
Yes. Many of the new hires
 are highly talented.

14:08.890 --> 14:10.320
I think we're in good shape.

14:10.320 --> 14:11.480
I'm glad.

14:11.830 --> 14:12.730
What's next?

14:12.730 --> 14:14.620
Do you want to stop by the shop?

14:14.620 --> 14:18.330
Not today. It looks pretty crowded.

14:18.330 --> 14:21.540
Understood. Will you be going
 straight home, then?

14:21.540 --> 14:23.500
That's the plan.

14:23.500 --> 14:26.720
You came all the way to the royal capital. 
Why not make a little detour?

14:27.100 --> 14:28.020
Huh?

14:28.680 --> 14:33.360
There's a newly opened café 
around here that's pretty popular.

14:33.360 --> 14:37.700
You can enjoy exotic imported tea there.

14:37.700 --> 14:40.400
It's been all the rage with the nobles lately.

14:42.230 --> 14:43.950
<i>How interesting.</i>

14:47.140 --> 14:52.320
<i>But the commander is currently 
here as my bodyguard...</i>

14:52.320 --> 14:55.730
<i>I would feel bad dragging him 
around the capital.</i>

14:55.730 --> 14:57.500
Where is it?

14:59.870 --> 15:01.820
Go straight down this way.

15:01.820 --> 15:03.930
Then turn at the flower shop.

15:03.930 --> 15:09.870
Follow that road and you'll see it 
right across from a large pharmacy.

15:09.870 --> 15:14.210
You might spot the line for it
 as soon as you round the corner.

15:14.210 --> 15:16.060
Got it. Thank you.

15:16.060 --> 15:18.400
Um, Lord Hawke...

15:18.400 --> 15:19.950
Aren't you curious?

15:19.950 --> 15:20.890
Huh?

15:26.020 --> 15:26.820
Yes.

15:26.820 --> 15:29.270
Then let's stop by.

15:29.270 --> 15:31.890
Th-Thank you very much.

16:05.750 --> 16:06.770
Wow!

16:07.170 --> 16:08.670
Looks like this is the place.

16:13.730 --> 16:16.660
Welcome. Will it be a table for two today?

16:16.660 --> 16:18.030
Yes.

16:18.030 --> 16:19.790
Right this way, please.

16:36.430 --> 16:41.060
Excuse me. I heard that you have
exotic foreign tea here.

16:41.060 --> 16:44.820
Yes. Would you both like to order some?

16:46.750 --> 16:48.710
Yes, please.

16:48.710 --> 16:50.170
Coming right up.

16:56.750 --> 16:57.820
Sei?

16:57.820 --> 17:00.120
Oh, it's nothing.

17:11.920 --> 17:13.960
Thank you for waiting.

17:17.130 --> 17:22.060
This is our most recommended 
beverage, coffee.

17:22.420 --> 17:24.020
Coffee?!

17:26.050 --> 17:27.980
Is anything the matter?

17:27.980 --> 17:29.960
Oh, no! I'm sorry!

17:29.960 --> 17:32.860
It's nothing. I'm fine.

17:36.050 --> 17:37.550
Please take your time.

17:39.990 --> 17:41.400
Is something bothering you?

17:41.400 --> 17:45.840
I'm sorry. I was just surprised 
to see a drink I recognize.

17:45.840 --> 17:47.020
From your homeland?

17:47.020 --> 17:48.230
Yes.

17:59.710 --> 18:02.010
It has a stronger flavor than tea.

18:02.010 --> 18:05.570
I agree. It would be 
delicious with milk, too!

18:06.270 --> 18:09.070
Haven't you had this drink before, Sei?

18:09.070 --> 18:15.440
I have, but this version tastes different
from what I drank in Japan... back home.

18:15.440 --> 18:18.600
I think it has to do with 
the way it's been brewed.

18:20.290 --> 18:26.620
Coffee can taste different depending on how 
the beans are roasted and how it's percolated.

18:26.620 --> 18:29.720
Did you drink this a lot in Japan?

18:29.720 --> 18:35.290
Yes. There's a component in coffee 
that can chase away sleepiness.

18:35.290 --> 18:38.800
I had a habit of drinking it daily
 after meals.

18:40.190 --> 18:41.260
I see.

18:41.260 --> 18:43.770
I used to brew my own coffee as well.

18:43.770 --> 18:44.960
Yourself?

18:44.960 --> 18:49.230
Yes. I think I'd be able to do it with 
the right tools here, too.

18:50.690 --> 18:55.200
<i>But what could I use
to brew coffee over here?</i>

18:55.200 --> 19:00.160
<i>I remember seeing a drama where they
used beakers and flasks to make it...</i>

19:01.870 --> 19:06.690
<i>First, I should see
if this shop sells the beans.</i>

19:08.390 --> 19:10.560
I-I'm sorry! I couldn't help myself...

19:10.560 --> 19:12.290
Did you have an idea?

19:12.970 --> 19:14.000
Huh?

19:14.950 --> 19:16.680
I'm looking forward to it.

19:32.710 --> 19:35.820
Director, are you drinking more?

19:35.820 --> 19:37.280
Don't be like that.

19:37.280 --> 19:39.530
I'm paying for the beans myself.

19:40.740 --> 19:44.280
I know. That's not what I'm getting at.

19:44.280 --> 19:46.500
It's not healthy to drink too much.

19:46.500 --> 19:49.910
Caffeine poisoning was a very real thing
back in Japan.

19:50.240 --> 19:51.890
Please don't overdo it.

19:51.890 --> 19:54.130
I got it, I got it. I'll be careful.

19:54.680 --> 19:57.930
There's no way I could really drink enough 
to poison myself, right?

19:57.930 --> 19:59.940
Well, that's true.

19:59.940 --> 20:01.600
Oh, there you are!

20:11.130 --> 20:14.130
I can't believe the café you visited
on a random suggestion

20:14.130 --> 20:16.500
had a drink that existed 
in your previous world.

20:16.500 --> 20:17.890
What a coincidence!

20:17.890 --> 20:20.160
I know. I was really surprised.

20:20.540 --> 20:26.330
Didn't you say that there are 
other familiar things here too, Sei?

20:26.330 --> 20:27.370
That's right.

20:27.370 --> 20:32.730
Then there might be more here
from your world than we realize.

20:32.730 --> 20:34.330
I sure hope so.

20:34.330 --> 20:37.420
<i>What I really want right now is rice.</i>

20:37.420 --> 20:40.630
What other kinds of things 
do you think we might have?

20:40.630 --> 20:42.440
Well...

20:42.440 --> 20:46.510
I'm not sure, but I want to 
search for rice in this world.

20:46.510 --> 20:48.020
Ryce?

20:48.020 --> 20:49.390
What about the paddy plant?

20:49.390 --> 20:50.390
Pahdi plant?

20:50.390 --> 20:52.130
The whole plant is called a paddy.

20:52.130 --> 20:57.110
The seed it produces is called rice. 
They refer to the same plant.

20:58.860 --> 21:03.820
In Japan, the country where I lived, 
it was the most consumed staple crop.

21:04.490 --> 21:06.880
I've never heard of it.

21:06.880 --> 21:08.390
I see...

21:08.390 --> 21:11.970
Maybe you should ask Franz about it.

21:11.970 --> 21:13.860
Franz, you say?

21:13.860 --> 21:18.150
He's traveled all over the world for work.

21:18.150 --> 21:20.280
He might know something about it.

21:20.280 --> 21:21.400
Other than that...

21:21.400 --> 21:23.410
Morgenhaffen is probably your best bet.

21:23.410 --> 21:25.260
Morgenhaffen?

21:25.260 --> 21:28.470
It's a large port city in the east.

21:28.890 --> 21:32.430
It's the trade destination of Salutania.

21:34.140 --> 21:37.520
There's a good chance you 
can find products there

21:37.520 --> 21:40.590
that aren't normally 
sold in the royal capital.

21:40.590 --> 21:41.610
Absolutely.

21:43.550 --> 21:46.700
<i>I've long given up on rice since coming here.</i>

21:46.700 --> 21:49.630
<i>But I'd love to have some again...</i>

21:51.690 --> 21:53.020
Want to go?

21:58.790 --> 22:02.050
Want to take a trip to Morgenhaffen?

22:04.160 --> 22:05.050
I do!

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Next Time

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
"A Foreign Country"
